---
/**
 * Privacy Policy.
 *
 * Written to describe what THIS site actually does, not a generic boilerplate:
 *  - the Get-in-Touch form collects name / email / phone / message and forwards
 *    them to AgencyBloc (the CRM) via /api/lead;
 *  - the optional Step-2 scheduler is a cal.com embed, loaded only if used;
 *  - homepage reviews are pulled from Google at BUILD time (no visitor tracking);
 *  - fonts are self-hosted; there are no advertising or analytics trackers.
 *
 * REVIEW BEFORE LAUNCH (owner / compliance / counsel):
 *  - Have Lisa / her compliance contact confirm the data-sharing and retention
 *    descriptions against her actual AgencyBloc setup and carrier agreements.
 *  - If analytics (e.g. Vercel Analytics, GA) or a mailing-list tool are added
 *    later, disclose them in "Cookies and tracking" / "Information I collect".
 *  - Confirm whether a physical mailing address should be listed for requests.
 *  - This is a strong, accurate starting draft; it is not a substitute for legal
 *    review. Nothing here invents a fact about Lisa's business.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Lisa’s Insurance Agency';
const description =
  'How Lisa’s Insurance Agency collects, uses, shares and protects the information you provide, and the choices you have.';

/** Kept in code so the shown date and the <time> attribute never drift. */
const effectiveISO = '2026-09-19';
const effectiveLabel = 'September 19, 2026';
---

<Page
  title={title}
  description={description}
  rawTitle
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  intro="This policy explains what information I collect when you use this website or contact me, how I use it, and the choices you have."
>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="privacy-body-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The details</p>
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="privacy-body-heading">Your information, and what I do with it.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>Effective date:</strong>
          <time datetime={effectiveISO}>{effectiveLabel}</time>
        </p>
        <p>
          Lisa’s Insurance Agency (“I”, “me”, “my”) respects your privacy. This
          policy applies to
          <a href="https://www.lisasinsuranceagency.com">lisasinsuranceagency.com</a>
          and to the information you share with me when you ask for help with
          insurance.
        </p>

        <h3>Information I collect</h3>
        <p>
          I only collect what you choose to give me. When you use the contact
          form on this site, that is your <strong>name, email address, phone
          number, and whatever you write in the message</strong>. If you call,
          text or email me, I keep the information you share so I can help you.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site does not use advertising trackers, and I do not buy or sell
          personal information.
        </p>

        <h3>How I use your information</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>To respond to you and answer your questions.</li>
          <li>To compare plans and prepare quotes for the coverage you ask about.</li>
          <li>To help you apply for and enrol in a plan, if you choose to.</li>
          <li>To stay in touch about your coverage while you are my client.</li>
          <li>To meet the record-keeping rules that apply to licensed agents.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Calls and text messages</h3>
        <p>
          When you give me your phone number and ask to be contacted, you agree
          that I may call or text you about your request and your coverage.
          Message and data rates may apply. You can opt out of text messages at
          any time by replying STOP, and you can ask me to stop calling at any
          time.
        </p>

        <h3>When I share information, and with whom</h3>
        <p>I share your information only as needed to help you, or as the law requires:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Insurance carriers</strong> — to request quotes and submit
            applications for the coverage you choose.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Service providers who work on my behalf</strong> — for
            example, the customer-management system I use to keep track of client
            requests, and the scheduling tool that powers the “pick a time”
            calendar. They may only use your information to provide their service
            to me.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>When required</strong> — to comply with the law, a regulator,
            or a lawful request, or to protect rights and safety.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          I do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information, and I do not
          share it for anyone else’s marketing.
        </p>

        <h3>Cookies and tracking</h3>
        <p>
          This website does not set advertising or analytics cookies of its own.
          If you open the optional scheduling calendar, that feature is provided
          by a third party (cal.com) and may set its own cookies so it can work;
          that is the only place a cookie is involved, and only if you use it.
        </p>

        <h3>Reviews shown on this site</h3>
        <p>
          The reviews on the homepage come from my public Google Business
          listing and are shown exactly as they were written. They are collected
          when the site is built, not by tracking you.
        </p>

        <h3>How I protect your information</h3>
        <p>
          I take reasonable steps to keep your information secure. The contact
          form is transmitted over an encrypted connection and handed to my
          customer-management system on the server side; your details are never
          posted to a third party from your browser. No method of transmission
          or storage is completely secure, but I treat your information with care.
        </p>

        <h3>How long I keep it</h3>
        <p>
          I keep your information for as long as needed to help you and to meet
          the record-keeping requirements that apply to licensed insurance
          agents, after which it is removed or retained only as the law allows.
        </p>

        <h3>Your choices</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Ask me what information I have about you.</li>
          <li>Ask me to correct or update it.</li>
          <li>Ask me to delete it, where I am not required to keep it.</li>
          <li>Opt out of calls or texts at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To make any of these requests, just contact me using the details below.</p>

        <h3>Children’s privacy</h3>
        <p>
          This site is meant for adults seeking insurance. I do not knowingly
          collect information from children.
        </p>

        <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, I will post the updated version here with a new
          effective date.
        </p>

        <h3>Contact me</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a></li>
          <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="microline">Calling connects you with Lisa, a licensed insurance agent.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Questions about your information?"
    copy="Ask me anything about how I handle your details — I’m happy to walk you through it."
  />
</Page>
